  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed crossover will result in the intensity of vehicle movements onto the classified road leading to vehicles stopping, slowing and turning from, or onto Bury Street West, thus adversely affecting highway safety and prejudicial to the free and safe flow of traffic, including buses, pedestrians and cyclists, where alternative access does appear to be available. Further, a newly installed streetlamp directly outside the property presents a fixed physical constraint. Furthermore, the proposal not demonstrate sufficient separation from the existing street tree and would therefore compromise the health of the street tree and the subsequent long term survival of the tree.  The proposed removal of a front garden would also be out of keeping with the surrounding area. In these respects, the proposal would therefore be contrary to Core Strategy (2010) Policies CP24, CP25 and CP30 and Development Management Document Policies (2014) DMD37, DMD45, and DMD46 as well as the Council's Technical Footway Guidance (2013), and the aims of the NPPF."
